                %li
                  %a{:href => "#blackfold_approach"} Blackfold approach
                %li
                  %a{:href => "#ReferencesMicroscopicAdSCFTViapBraneSigmaModesl"}
                    Microscopic AdS/CFT via
                    = succeed "-brane" do
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %mi p
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            The theory of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gravity"} gravity
            in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn 3
                  %mo +
                  %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 3+1
            dimensions famously has
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/black+hole"} black hole
            solutions, being the limiting configuration of a
            %em point
            mass gravitational source. In higher dimensional gravity, and in particular in higher dimensional
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supergravity"} supergravity
            %em
              black
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/membrane"} membrane
            solutions hence generally of
            %em black brane
            solutions.
          %p
            Particularly the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/BPS+states"} BPS states
            among the black branes in
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supergravity"} supergravity
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Killing+spinors"} Killing spinors
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Green-Schwarz+super+p-branes"} Green-Schwarz super p-branes
          %div
            %p
              %strong>
                1/2
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/BPS+state"} BPS
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/black+branes"} black branes
                in
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supergravity"} supergravity
              \:
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D-branes"} D-branes
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/F1-brane"} F1-brane
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/NS5-brane"} NS5-brane
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M2-brane"} M2-brane
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M5-brane"} M5-brane
            %p
              %img{:src => "http://ncatlab.org/nlab/files/BraneSolutionsInSupergravity.jpg", :width => "600"}/
            %blockquote
              %p
                (table from
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "black+brane#BlumenhagenLustTheisen13"} Blumenhagen, Lüst &amp; Theisen 2013, Chapter 18.5
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/near-horizon+geometry"} near-horizon geometry
            of these black branes is generically that of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/anti+de+Sitter+spacetime"} anti de Sitter spacetime
            times a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sphere"} sphere
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/worldvolume"} worldvolume
            theory of the branes is a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/superconformal+QFT"} superconformal QFT
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/AdS-CFT+correspondence"} AdS-CFT correspondence
          %h2#properties Properties
          %h3#weak_coupling_correspondence Weak coupling correspondence
          %p
            The types of black branes that can occur in theories of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supergravity"} supergravity
            that are obtained from the maximal
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/11-dimensional+supergravity"} 11-dimensional supergravity
            match precisely the types of
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D-brane"} D-brane
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/NS-brane"} NS-brane
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/superstring+theories"} superstring theories
          %p The idea is that both these brane-phenomena are aspects of one single entity:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                At low
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string+coupling"} string coupling
                the
                = succeed "/" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D-brane"} D-brane
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/NS-brane"} NS-brane
                description is accurate. Low
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string+coupling"} string coupling
                implies that the coupling of
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gravity"} gravity
                is weak, hence that the back-reaction of the branes on the background geometry is negligible.
            %li
              %p
                At large
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string+coupling"} string coupling
                but low
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/energy"} energy
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/effective+field+theory"} effective
