          %h2#References References
          %p
            By “black branes” one mostly refers to – generally higher-dimensional – singular solutions of theories of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supergravity"} supergravity
          %ul
            %li
              %em
                %a{:href => "#ReferencesGeneral"} Black branes in supergravity
          %p
            But closely related discussion has historically been had on the possibility of identifying
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/electrons"} electrons
            and other
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fundamental+particles"} fundamental particles
            with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kerr-Newman+black+hole"} Kerr-Newman
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/black+holes"} black holes
            (“black 0-branes”):
          %div
            %h3#ReferencesMatchingKNBlackHolesToElementaryParticles Matching KN black holes to elementary particles
            %p
              On the similarity between
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kerr-Newman+black+holes"} Kerr-Newman black holes
              (charged and spinning “
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/black+brane"}> black 0-branes
              ”) and
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/elementary+particles"} elementary particles
              (
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+p-brane"}> sigma-model 0-branes
              ) like
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/electrons"} electrons
            %p
              Historical precursor discussion on the possibility of
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometrodynamics"} geometrodynamics
              for
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fundamental+particles"} fundamental particles
            %ul
              %li#EinsteinInfeldHoffmann39
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Albert+Einstein"}> Albert Einstein
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Leopold+Infeld"} Leopold Infeld
                = succeed "," do
                  %em The gravitational equations and the problem of motion
                %strong 39
                1 (1938) [
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.2307/1968714"}> doi:10.2307/1968714
                ,
                = succeed "]" do
                  %a{:href => "https://www.jstor.org/stable/1968714"} jstor:1968714
            %p
              Seminal observation that the gyromagnetic ratio of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kerr-Newman+black+hole"} Kerr-Newman black hole
              is 2, just as the for
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/electron"} electron
              (cf. at
              = succeed "):" do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/anomalous+magnetic+moment"} anomalous magnetic moment
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  Brandon Carter, p. 1562 of:
                  = succeed "," do
                    %em Global Structure of the Kerr Family of Gravitational Fields
                  %strong 174
                  (1968) 1559 [
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1103/PhysRev.174.1559"}> doi:10.1103/PhysRev.174.1559
                  ]
              %li
                %p
                  Werner Israel,
                  = succeed "," do
                    %em Source of the Kerr Metric
                  %strong 2
                  641 (1970) [
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1103/PhysRevD.2.641"}> doi:10.1103/PhysRevD.2.641
                  ]
            %p Further discussion:
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  Carlos A. López,
                  = succeed "," do
                    %em Extended model of the electron in general relativity
                  %strong 30
                  313 (1984) [
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1103/PhysRevD.30.313"} doi:10.1103/PhysRevD.30.313
                  %a ]
              %li
                %p
                  H. I. Arcos, J. G. Pereira:
                  = succeed "," do
                    %em Kerr–Newman Solution as a Dirac Particle
                  %strong 36
                  (2004) 2441–2464 [
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1023/B:GERG.0000046832.71368.a5"}> doi:10.1023/B:GERG.0000046832.71368.a5
                  ,
                  = succeed "]" do
                    %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/0210103"} arXiv:hep-th/0210103
              %li
                %p
                  Alexander Burinskii,
                  = succeed "," do
                    %em The Dirac-Kerr-Newman electron
                  %strong 14
                  (2008) 109–122 [
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1134/S0202289308020011"}> doi:10.1134/S0202289308020011
                  ,
                  = succeed "]" do
                    %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/0507109"} arXiv:hep-th/0507109
              %li
                %p
                  Alexander Burinskii,
                  = succeed "," do
                    %em Kerr–Newman electron as spinning soliton
                  %strong 29
                  26, 1450133 (2014) [
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1142/S0217751X14501334"}> doi:10.1142/S0217751X14501334
                  ,
                  = succeed "]" do
                    %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1410.2888"} arXiv:1410.2888
            %p See also:
            %ul
              %li
                Wikipedia,
                %em
                  %a{:href => "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Black_hole_electron"} Black hole electron
          %h3#ReferencesGeneral Black branes in supergravity
          %p
            Original articles on black branes in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supergravity"} supergravity
            (and thereby in
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string+theory"} string
            = succeed "):" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M-theory"} M-theory
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Michael+Duff"}> Michael Duff
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ramzi+R.+Khuri"} Ramzi R. Khuri
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jian+Xin+Lu"} Jian Xin Lu
                = succeed "," do
                  %em String and Fivebrane Solitons: Singular or Non-singular?
                %strong 377
                (1992) 281-294 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9112023"}> arXiv:hep-th/9112023
                ,
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1016/0550-3213(92)90025-7"} doi:10.1016/0550-3213(92)90025-7
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Michael+Duff"}> Michael Duff
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jian+Xin+Lu"} Jian Xin Lu
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    Black and super
                    = succeed "-branes" do
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %mi p
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
                %strong 416
                (1994) 301-334 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9306052"}> arXiv:hep-th/9306052
                ,
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1016/0550-3213(94)90586-X"} doi:10.1016/0550-3213(94)90586-X
            %li#DuffKhuriLu94
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mike+Duff"}> Mike Duff
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ramzi+R.+Khuri"} Ramzi R. Khuri
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jian+Xin+Lu"} Jian Xin Lu
                = succeed "," do
                  %em String Solitons
                %strong 259
                (1995) 213-326 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9412184"}> arXiv:hep-th/9412184
                ,
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1016/0370-1573(95)00002-X"} doi:10.1016/0370-1573(95)00002-X
              %blockquote
                %p
                  (
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/solitonic+branes"}> solitonic branes
                  )
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Michael+Duff"}> Michael Duff
                , H. Lu,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Christopher+Pope"} Christopher Pope
                = succeed "," do
                  %em The Black Branes of M-theory
                %strong 382
                (1996) &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9604052"}> arXiv:hep-th/9604052
                \&amp;rbrack;
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M5-brane"} M5-brane
            was maybe first found as a black brane of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/11-dimensional+supergravity"} 11-dimensional supergravity
            (the
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/black+fivebrane"} black fivebrane
          %ul
            %li#Gueven92
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Rahmi+Gueven"}> Rahmi Gueven
              ,
              %em
                Black
                = succeed "-brane" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi p
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi D
                      %mo =
                      %mn 11
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D = 11
                supergravity theory, Phys. Lett. B276 (1992) 49 and in
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mike+Duff"} Mike Duff
                (ed.)
              = succeed "_" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/The+World+in+Eleven+Dimensions"} The World in Eleven Dimensions
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://inspirehep.net/record/338203"} spire:338203
          %p
            The observation that black
            = succeed "-branes" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
            %em odd
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi p
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
            are completely non-singular is due to
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Gary+Gibbons"}> Gary Gibbons
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Gary+Horowitz"} Gary Horowitz
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Paul+Townsend"} Paul Townsend
              = succeed "," do
                %em Higher-dimensional resolution of dilatonic black hole singularities
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9410073"} arXiv:hep-th/9410073
          %p
            The suggestion that extremal/
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/BPS+state"} BPS state
            black branes are the strong coupling incarnation of fundamental branes originates in
          %ul
            %li#HullTownsend94
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chris+Hull"}> Chris Hull
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Paul+Townsend"} Paul Townsend
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Unity of Superstring Dualities
                %strong 438
                (1995) 109-137 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9410167"}> arXiv:hep-th/9410167
                \&amp;rbrack;
            %li#Witten95
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Edward+Witten"}> Edward Witten
                , p. 6 (bottom) of:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em String Theory Dynamics In Various Dimensions
                %strong 443
                (1995) 85-126 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9503124"}> arXiv:hep-th/9503124
                \&amp;rbrack;
          %p Review:
          %ul
            %li#Duff99
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mike+Duff"}> Mike Duff
                , chapter 5 of:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/The+World+in+Eleven+Dimensions"}> The World in Eleven Dimensions
                    \: Supergravity, Supermembranes and M-theory
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://www.crcpress.com/The-World-in-Eleven-Dimensions-Supergravity-supermembranes-and-M-theory/Duff/9780750306720"} ISBN:9780750306720
            %li#Stelle98
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kellogg+Stelle"}> Kellogg Stelle
                , around section 3.3 of:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em BPS Branes in Supergravity
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Quantum Field Theory: Perspective and Prospective
                %strong 530
                (1999) 257-351 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9803116"}> arXiv:hep-th/9803116
                ,
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/978-94-011-4542-8_12"} doi:10.1007/978-94-011-4542-8_12
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ofer+Aharony"}> Ofer Aharony
                , S. S. Gubser,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Juan+Maldacena"} Juan Maldacena
                %em Large N Field Theories, String Theory and Gravity
                \&amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9905111"}> arXiv:hep-th/9905111
                \&amp;rbrack;
            %li#Mohaupt00
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Thomas+Mohaupt"}> Thomas Mohaupt
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Black holes in supergravity and string theory
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://www.itp.uni-hannover.de/~giulini/papers/BlackHoleSeminar/Mohaupt_CQG_2000.pdf"} pdf
            %li#BlumenhagenLustTheisen13
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ralph+Blumenhagen"}> Ralph Blumenhagen
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dieter+L%C3%BCst"} Dieter Lüst
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Stefan+Theisen"} Stefan Theisen
                = succeed "," do
